From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] config: read the system bat config from all three UAPI paths
Source: no upstream commit; written for Nex against bat 0.26.1
Upstream: not submitted. get_args_from_config_file() reads a single fixed
 path from system_config_file() (/etc/bat/config), so a distribution cannot
 ship a default that a boot or an administrator may replace.

get_args_from_config_file() concatenates the system config file, then the
user config file, in that order; get_args_from_str() applies later flags
over earlier ones, so a later line in the concatenated text wins. There is
no vendor or runtime tier, so a distribution cannot ship a default
configuration below /usr, and a running system cannot install a temporary
override below /run: only a persistent /etc file works.

Before the existing system_config_file() (/etc/bat/config) read, read
/usr/lib/bat/config, then /run/bat/config, keeping the same
concatenate-in-order behavior so an administrator file still overrides a
runtime file, which still overrides a vendor file. The user config file
(BAT_CONFIG_PATH or XDG) still overrides all three system tiers, and
BAT_OPTS is untouched.

diff -urN a/src/bin/bat/config.rs b/src/bin/bat/config.rs
--- a/src/bin/bat/config.rs
+++ b/src/bin/bat/config.rs
@@ -104,9 +104,15 @@
 pub fn get_args_from_config_file() -> Result<Vec<OsString>, shell_words::ParseError> {
     let mut config = String::new();

-    if let Ok(c) = fs::read_to_string(system_config_file()) {
-        config.push_str(&c);
-        config.push('\n');
+    for tier_path in [
+        PathBuf::from("/usr/lib/bat/config"),
+        PathBuf::from("/run/bat/config"),
+        system_config_file(),
+    ] {
+        if let Ok(c) = fs::read_to_string(tier_path) {
+            config.push_str(&c);
+            config.push('\n');
+        }
     }

     if let Ok(c) = fs::read_to_string(config_file()) {
